### Name and Version

PrismML-Eng/llama.cpp prism-b10709-9a9394a (9a9394a895b96003ca842a6041cb28ac49a108f7), bundled llama-ui. Model: Qwen/Qwen3-8B-GGUF, Qwen3-8B-Q4_K_M.gguf. Not yet reproduced on current upstream.

### Operating systems

Windows

### Which llama.cpp modules do you know to be affected?

llama-server

### Command line

```shell
llama-server -m Qwen3-8B-Q4_K_M.gguf --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8080 -ngl 99 -c 8192 -np 1 -b 128 -ub 128 -fa on --jinja --temp 1 --top-p 0.95 --top-k 20 --min-p 0 --reasoning-budget 0
```

### Problem description & steps to reproduce

Related: #26540 (closed automatically for inactivity).

A continuously rotating CSS spinner reduces local CUDA generation throughput even on a standalone page without llama-ui, Svelte, or Markdown. In bundled llama-ui, stopping only the loading spinner improved throughput from about 42 to 52.82 tokens/s.

### Environment and limitations

Windows 10 Pro; i7-11800H; 32GB RAM; RTX 3070 Laptop 8GB; NVIDIA driver 610.62; Codex in-app Chromium browser. Backend/model/version and flags are listed above. **Not reproduced on current upstream, standalone Chrome/Edge, or another OS yet.** This may involve browser/GPU scheduling or resource contention; the exact mechanism and whether upstream is affected remain unconfirmed.

### Measurements

Each case uses the same prompt, seed 42, 384 output tokens, thinking disabled, and cache_prompt=false. Cases run sequentially. Speeds are backend timings.predicted_per_second, not browser paint timing. These are single runs with a repeated baseline, not a statistical benchmark.

| Rendering mode | Backend tokens/s |
| --- | ---: |
| Consume SSE without output updates | 59.40 |
| Only a 20px rotating CSS spinner | 44.95 |
| Plain text update per event, no spinner | 54.06 |
| Plain text update at most every 100ms, no spinner | 58.75 |
| Plain text per event plus spinner | 44.08 |
| Repeat no-output baseline | 57.95 |

In actual llama-ui, applying `.loading-icon.animate-spin { animation: none !important; }` via Custom CSS yielded 52.82 tokens/s over 720 tokens with normal text streaming. Computed animation-name was verified as none; console had no warnings/errors. The rotating Loader2 is in tools/ui/src/lib/components/app/chat/ChatTabs/ChatTabsItem.svelte in the tested revision.

### Reproduce

1. Run the local CUDA server on 127.0.0.1:8080 with the model/flags above and no concurrent inference requests.
2. Save the complete code below as render-bench.mjs. Tested with Node 18.19.1, no npm dependencies.
3. Run `node render-bench.mjs`.
4. Open http://127.0.0.1:8081 and click Run tests. Keep the page visible for all six cases.
5. Compare the backend speeds. Stop the diagnostic server with Ctrl+C.

The script listens only on loopback, proxies only local chat completions, and sends no data externally. It assumes the backend does not require an API key.

<details>
<summary>Complete render-bench.mjs</summary>

```javascript
import http from 'node:http';
const html = `<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Local rendering benchmark</title>
<style>body{font:16px sans-serif;margin:30px}#spinner{width:20px;height:20px;border:3px solid #aaa;border-top-color:#06f;border-radius:50%;visibility:hidden} .spin{animation:spin 1s linear infinite} @keyframes spin{to{transform:rotate(360deg)}} pre{white-space:pre-wrap;max-width:900px}td,th{padding:6px;border:1px solid #bbb}</style>
<h1>Local rendering benchmark</h1><p>Same local model and request. Tests run sequentially. No remote data transfer.</p><button id="run">Run tests</button><p id="state">Ready</p><div id="spinner"></div><table><thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Tokens/s</th><th>Tokens</th><th>Wall seconds</th></tr></thead><tbody id="results"></tbody></table><pre id="output"></pre>
<script>
const prompt='请写一篇1500字的中文科幻故事：一名维修工程师在月球基地发现一段来自未来的求救信息。请直接开始正文，包含人物对话和具体场景，不要写提纲。';
const modes=['no-render','spinner-only','per-token','batched-100ms','per-token-spinner','no-render-repeat'];
document.querySelector('#run').onclick=async()=>{
document.querySelector('#run').disabled=true;
try { for(const mode of modes){
document.querySelector('#state').textContent='Running '+mode;
const spinner=document.querySelector('#spinner'); spinner.style.visibility=mode.includes('spinner')?'visible':'hidden'; spinner.className=mode.includes('spinner')?'spin':'';
const out=document.querySelector('#output');out.textContent=''; let text='', last=0, timings,usage;
const start=performance.now();
const response=await fetch('/v1/chat/completions',{method:'POST',headers:{'Content-Type':'application/json'},body:JSON.stringify({messages:[{role:'user',content:prompt}],max_tokens:384,temperature:1,seed:42,chat_template_kwargs:{enable_thinking:false},stream:true,stream_options:{include_usage:true},cache_prompt:false})});
if(!response.ok)throw new Error(await response.text());
const reader=response.body.getReader(), decoder=new TextDecoder();let buffer='';
while(true){const {done,value}=await reader.read();if(done)break;buffer+=decoder.decode(value,{stream:true});const lines=buffer.split('\\n');buffer=lines.pop();for(const line of lines){if(!line.startsWith('data: ')||line==='data: [DONE]')continue;const event=JSON.parse(line.slice(6));if(event.timings)timings=event.timings;if(event.usage)usage=event.usage;text+=event.choices?.[0]?.delta?.content||'';if(mode.startsWith('per-token')||(mode==='batched-100ms'&&performance.now()-last>=100)){out.textContent=text;last=performance.now()}}}
const row=document.querySelector('#results').insertRow();for(const val of [mode,timings?.predicted_per_second?.toFixed(2),usage?.completion_tokens,((performance.now()-start)/1000).toFixed(2)])row.insertCell().textContent=val;
} document.querySelector('#state').textContent='Complete';}catch(e){document.querySelector('#state').textContent='Error: '+e.message}finally{document.querySelector('#spinner').className='';document.querySelector('#run').disabled=false}
};
</script>`;
